{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"06cf56bcc6eb941a52d9fb7a741c47df","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see - the linter reformatted my `prCreateArgs` into this awkward form where `args = append([]string{...})` - the append is useless here since we're just assigning the result of appending nothing to `args`. This is what the linter/goimports-reviser produced after formatting.\n\nThe fix should be to just conditionally add `--draft` to the args list, rather than rebuilding the whole list. Let me rewrite `prCreateArgs` cleanly:\n\n```go\nfunc prCreateArgs(base, head, title, body string, target PRTarget) []string {\n    args := []string{\"pr\", \"create\"}\n    if target.IsDraft() {\n        args = append(args, \"--draft\")\n    }\n    args = append(args, \"--base\", base, \"--head\", head, \"--title\", title, \"--body\", body)\n    return args\n}\n```\n\nThis is cleaner and avoids the lint issue.","signature":"7cfa89bbfe1556604bf7c2fc49a220b144d21cf61c59054ff7c5f1e3ef7f1eb8"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":66292,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":23786},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef341d7c-598a-44a9-af65-46186c69de29","uuid":"b860b1f5-61fb-4521-9d86-c85caa236962","timestamp":"2026-08-15T08:30:57.565Z"}
